72.9 million, with Bamboo Hills Residences, Duo Tower, Aster Hill, and Laurel Residence accounting for the majority of sales.\n\n# UOA Development FY2025 Net Profit Jumps To RM474 Mln\n\n25/02/2026 08:11 PM\n\nImage\n\nKUALA LUMPUR, Feb 25 (Bernama) -- UOA Development Bhd's net profit rose to RM474.04 million for the financial year ended Dec 31, 2025 (FY2025) from RM287.30 million in the preceding year.\n\nThe property developer group’s revenue also expanded to RM674.28 million compared with RM545.69 million in FY2024.\n\nFor the fourth quarter (4Q) of FY2025, UOA Development recorded a higher net profit of RM192.75 million versus RM128.20 million in 4Q FY2024; however, its revenue fell to RM174.72 million from RM234.86 million previously.\n\nThe group said the bigger net profit was primarily attributed to the higher fair value adjustment on investment properties, while the higher revenue was supported by the progressive recognition of the group's ongoing development projects, namely Bamboo Hills Residences, the medical centre in Bangsar South, Aster Hill, and Duo Tower.\n\nOn its prospects, UOA Development said its new property sales for the period ending Dec 31, 2025, totalled at RM672.9 million, with Bamboo Hills Residences, Duo Tower, Aster Hill, and Laurel Residence accounting for the majority of sales.\n\n\"Unbilled sales amounted to RM656.5 million at quarter-end, which will be recognised progressively in the coming years. In view of these, the group continues to explore strategic land parcels that align with and amplify the group’s objectives,\" it added.\n\n-- BERNAMA\n\n KEYWORDS\n\nuoa development fy2025 corporate\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUOADEV - Annual Report | KLSE Screener (https://www.klsescreener.com/v2/announcements/stock/5200?category=AR)\nciteturn361search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; 27 Apr UOA DEVELOPMENT BHD Annual Report 9:11 am Annual Report & CG Report - 2025 29 Apr UOA DE